[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two pumpkin spice oat mug cakes are centered in the frame, placed side-by-side on a rustic, aged oak wood surface, leaving enough negative space for a circular crop. Shot from a 3/4 overhead angle, roughly 40 degrees, ensuring the interior texture of both cakes is visible. Shallow depth of field keeps the primary mug in sharp focus while the second mug is softly blurred in the background. Soft, natural side light from a window to the left creates gentle, realistic shadows and highlights the moist, slightly spongy texture of the warm cakes. Each mug cake is topped with a generous, slightly uneven dollop of thick, white, nonfat plain Greek yogurt that is just beginning to soften from the residual heat. A scattering of finely chopped, rustic-cut pecans sits on top of the yogurt. The cakes appear dense, amber-orange in color, with a slight puff and visible flecks of pumpkin pie spice throughout. A single, small wooden spoon rests casually on the wood surface near one of the mugs. A few stray pecan pieces and a faint dusting of oat flour are scattered naturally on the table. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: a small smudge of yogurt on the inner rim of one mug, slightly uneven cake surface, and a crumb trail on the wood. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces. Warm, golden-hour color temperature—cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
